ed allelic and phenotypic heterogeneity of GSD III in our country [11]. We used different types of GSD in the", "has_full_abstract": true, "main_abstract_source": "publisher_page", "gs_use_publisher_full_abstract": false, "title_refetch_main_abstract_source": "bibtex", "abstract_supplemented_by_title_query": true}}

